      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, I can delve deeper into those stereotypes with a sharper edge. Here's my take:\n\n1. Italian-American Christmas Eve: It's either Macaroni & Cheese or Blood Wars over Grandma's meatloaf—where's the middle ground at Casa Capalbo?\n\n2. Irish-American marriage: A perfect volatile marriage at 31: Joey, Cork, or Rosie. Pick your family's favorite disaster—Fit 4 Two or Awkward Family Gathering?\n\n3. Crime drama tropes intersecting cultures—Italian-Americans in church business dinners, Irish-Americans in pubs with banana skins—shocked the Vatican, burnt down the pub.\n\n4. How to tell an Italian-American from an Irish-American: The former says \"What is that tragic expression?\" with this perplexing grimace resembling the Mona Lisa circa 1503. The latter thinks it’s the curtain in a show about rift/separation.\n\n5. The gag you didn't know: Italian-Americans: Always say \"Brenda\" at the bakery but wear actual clothes. Irish-Americans: Same principle—brie with rosemary on a cereal box but without communal guilt. And the universal truth? Both deal with law enforcement justifying a family member's getaway incident. The differences? Spoiler alert:",
